s.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"prop\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bd43bf9e-9099-4436-9e3e-9111b468519e\" />\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nI didn't find an issue related to this; the idea came from my workflow on my projects.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nAdds two new toolbar buttons to the 2D and 3D editors:\r\n\r\n- Lock multiple children\r\n- Unlock multiple children\r\n\r\nThese actions recursively lock or unlock the selected node and all of its descendants, making it easier to manage complex scene hierarchies. Child nodes are managed independently from their own children. Locking or unlocking a parent node only affects its direct children. To modify deeper descendants, select those nodes separately. This approach provides finer control over which parts of the scene hierarchy are locked or unlocked.\r\n\r\nThis complements the existing lock/unlock functionality for individual nodes.\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","descr